WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.550
GROUPING SETS gives you explicit control over which
summary levels are returned

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:10.799
Instead of generating a fixed hierarchy or every
possible combination you list

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:15.885
the groupings you actually need Run this example and
look at the

00:00:15.898 --> 00:00:21.619
report levels Compare them with ROLLUP and CUBE This

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:25.212
feature is useful when a report needs only selected
totals such as

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:31.000
category totals and a grand total but not every
product subtotal The

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:35.132
output still contains rows at different grains so
label or interpret those

00:00:35.158 --> 00:00:40.642
rows carefully Think of GROUPING SETS as a way to
ask PostgreSQL

00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:44.510
for several GROUP BY queries at once while keeping
the requested summary

00:00:44.536 --> 00:00:45.931
levels under your control
